  "section_notes": "S1 is strict and safe, requiring 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, 48-hour customer notice, and no cause-confirmation escape. S2 is weakened by a permanent 7% failure-rate cap with no automatic sales stop, letting Northwind's Hearth 10 pass while results reach customers but not the general public. S3 is weakened by the 24-month new-unit deadline, S4 is acceptable at 36 months, and S5 is acceptable with a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger but only prompt notice and no serious-injury clause."
